<speak>Perhaps how they end. I would find it useful if the closing part made clear whether there is an administrative question still open, rather than ending with a general invitation to get in touch. Sometimes that invitation is perfectly courteous, but I put the telephone down wondering whether I was expected to do something. I am not asking for a rehearsal of everything we have discussed. Just a clear distinction between something awaiting an answer and something that was merely part of the conversation.</speak>